      "description": "The first numbered response in a decision: ink fill, key hint beside the label.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-btn ds-btn-primary\">Go ahead<kbd class=\"ds-kbd\">1</kbd></button>",
      "css": ".ds-btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;height:34px;padding:0 14px;border:1.5px solid var(--text,#111111);border-radius:2px;background:transparent;color:var(--text,#111111);font:600 13.5px/1 var(--font-sans,'Archivo Variable',sans-serif);cursor:pointer;transition:background .15s,color .15s,transform .1s}.ds-btn-primary{background:var(--act,#111111);border-color:var(--act,#111111);color:var(--on-act,#ffffff)}.ds-btn-primary:hover{background:var(--act-hover,#34342f);border-color:var(--act-hover,#34342f)}.ds-btn:active{transform:translateY(1px)}.ds-btn:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent,#c8211a);outline-offset:2px}.ds-kbd{display:inline-grid;place-items:center;min-width:18px;height:18px;padding:0 4px;margin-left:2px;border-radius:2px;font:500 10.5px/1 var(--font-code,'Geist Mono',monospace);color:currentColor;opacity:.75;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px currentColor}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Outlined Response",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "button-secondary",
      "description": "The other numbered responses: a printed box with a 1.5px ink stroke.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-btn-o\">Change it<kbd class=\"ds-kbd-o\">2</kbd></button>",
      "css": ".ds-btn-o{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;height:34px;padding:0 14px;border:1.5px solid var(--text,#111111);border-radius:2px;background:transparent;color:var(--text,#111111);font:600 13.5px/1 var(--font-sans,'Archivo Variable',sans-serif);cursor:pointer;transition:background .15s,transform .1s}.ds-btn-o:hover{background:var(--surface-2,#f4f4f1)}.ds-btn-o:active{transform:translateY(1px)}.ds-btn-o:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent,#c8211a);outline-offset:2px}.ds-kbd-o{display:inline-grid;place-items:center;min-width:18px;height:18px;padding:0 4px;border-radius:2px;font:500 10.5px/1 var(--font-code,'Geist Mono',monospace);color:var(--text-3,#686862);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--line-2,#b8b8b0)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Ghost Button",
      "kind": "button",
      "refersTo": "button-ghost",
      "description": "Snooze and Cancel: no stroke, soft ink.",
      "html": "<button class=\"ds-btn-ghost\">Snooze</button>",
      "css": ".ds-btn-ghost{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:28px;padding:0 10px;border:1.5px solid transparent;border-radius:2px;background:transparent;color:var(--text-2,#45453f);font:600 12.5px/1 var(--font-sans,'Archivo Variable',sans-serif);cursor:pointer;transition:background .15s,color .15s}.ds-btn-ghost:hover{background:var(--surface-2,#f4f4f1);color:var(--text,#111111)}.ds-btn-ghost:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent,#c8211a);outline-offset:2px}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Reason Field",
      "kind": "input",
      "refersTo": "field",
      "description": "Textarea for the reason behind Change it, Take over or Not this; the ring turns ink on focus.",
      "html": "<textarea class=\"ds-field\" rows=\"2\" placeholder=\"One line is enough. BahnBot learns from it.\"></textarea>",
      "css": ".ds-field{width:320px;min-height:44px;padding:10px 12px;border:0;border-radius:2px;resize:vertical;font:400 14px/1.5 var(--font-sans,'Archivo Variable',sans-serif);color:var(--text,#111111);background:var(--surface,#ffffff);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1.5px var(--line-2,#b8b8b0);transition:box-shadow .15s}.ds-field::placeholder{color:var(--text-3,#686862)}.ds-field:focus{outline:0;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1.5px var(--text,#111111)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Header Bar",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "header-bar",
      "description": "The black timetable bar: red brand square, condensed wordmark, work links with a red current underline.",
      "html": "<header class=\"ds-bar\"><a class=\"ds-brand\" href=\"#\"><span class=\"ds-mark\"></span><span class=\"ds-name\">BahnOS</span></a><nav class=\"ds-nav\"><a class=\"ds-link\" aria-current=\"page\" href=\"#\">Today<span class=\"ds-count ds-hot\">19</span><span class=\"ds-line\"></span></a><a class=\"ds-link\" href=\"#\">Heads-up<span class=\"ds-count\">9</span></a><a class=\"ds-link\" href=\"#\">Ops map</a></nav></header>",
      "css": ".ds-bar{display:flex;align-items:stretch;gap:22px;height:52px;padding:0 20px;background:var(--bar,#111111);color:var(--bar-text,#f4f4f0);font-family:var(--font-sans,'Archivo Variable',sans-serif)}.ds-brand{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;color:inherit;text-decoration:none}.ds-mark{width:12px;height:12px;background:var(--accent,#c8211a)}.ds-name{font-stretch:75%;font-weight:750;font-size:20px;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase;line-height:1}.ds-nav{display:flex;align-items:stretch;gap:2px}.ds-link{position:relative;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;padding:0 10px;font:500 13.5px/1 var(--font-sans,'Archivo Variable',sans-serif);color:var(--bar-text-2,#a9a9a2);text-decoration:none;transition:color .15s}.ds-link:hover,.ds-link[aria-current=page]{color:var(--bar-text,#f4f4f0)}.ds-link:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent,#c8211a);outline-offset:-2px}.ds-line{position:absolute;left:10px;right:10px;bottom:0;height:3px;background:var(--accent,#c8211a)}.ds-count{min-width:20px;height:18px;padding:0 5px;display:inline-grid;place-items:center;font-size:11.5px;font-weight:650;color:var(--bar-text-2,#a9a9a2);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,.22)}.ds-hot{color:#fff;background:#c8211a;box-shadow:none}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Timetable Queue",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "queue-row",
      "description": "Head row with an opening 2px rule, then one order per row in a shared column rhythm; the selected row is the reversed plate.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-tt\"><div class=\"ds-tt-head\"><span>Order</span><span>Car and reason</span><span>Leg and next move</span><span>Due</span></div><button class=\"ds-qi\" aria-current=\"true\"><span class=\"ds-ref\">420322</span><span class=\"ds-main\"><b>Bentley Continental GT</b><span class=\"ds-why\">Red warning on the road</span></span><span class=\"ds-main\"><span>Munich → Hamburg</span><span class=\"ds-why\">Take over</span></span><span class=\"ds-side\"><span class=\"ds-due ds-late\">5 h</span><span class=\"ds-why\">Delivery promise</span></span></button><button class=\"ds-qi\"><span class=\"ds-ref\">420154</span><span class=\"ds-main\"><b>Audi Q8 e-tron</b><span class=\"ds-why\">Book travel for the driver</span></span><span class=\"ds-main\"><span>Marseille → Lahti</span><span class=\"ds-why\">Go ahead</span></span><span class=\"ds-side\"><span class=\"ds-due\">23 h</span><span class=\"ds-why\">Pickup slot</span></span></button></div>",
      "css": ".ds-tt{width:600px;font:400 14px/1.5 var(--font-sans,'Archivo Variable',sans-serif);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--text,#111111);background:var(--surface,#ffffff)}.ds-tt-head,.ds-qi{display:grid;grid-template-columns:64px minmax(0,1fr) 132px 100px;gap:14px}.ds-tt-head{padding:7px 16px;border-top:2px solid var(--rule,#111111);border-bottom:1px solid var(--rule,#111111);font-size:11.5px;font-weight:750;font-stretch:75%;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em}.ds-tt-head span:last-child{text-align:right}.ds-qi{width:100%;align-items:start;padding:11px 16px;border:0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line,#deded8);border-radius:0;background:transparent;color:inherit;font:inherit;text-align:left;cursor:pointer}.ds-qi:hover:not([aria-current]){background:var(--surface-2,#f4f4f1)}.ds-qi:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--accent,#c8211a);outline-offset:-2px}.ds-ref{font:500 12px/1.4 var(--font-code,'Geist Mono',monospace);color:var(--text-3,#686862);padding-top:2px}.ds-main{display:grid;gap:2px;min-width:0}.ds-main b{font-weight:650}.ds-why{font-size:13px;color:var(--text-2,#45453f);white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}.ds-side{display:grid;justify-items:end;gap:2px}.ds-due{font-size:17px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.2}.ds-late{color:var(--accent-text,#b21d17)}.ds-qi[aria-current]{background:var(--plate,#111111);color:var(--on-plate,#ffffff)}.ds-qi[aria-current] .ds-why{color:var(--on-plate-2,#c4c4bd)}.ds-qi[aria-current] .ds-ref,.ds-qi[aria-current] .ds-late{color:var(--plate-accent,#ff6b5e);font-weight:700}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Status Badge",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "badge",
      "description": "Printed status box; tone variants take the tone's text colour, a soft tint and a 45% ring.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-badge\">Estimate</span> <span class=\"ds-badge ds-badge-ok\"><span class=\"ds-dot\"></span>Booked</span> <span class=\"ds-badge ds-badge-warn\"><span class=\"ds-dot\"></span>On watch</span>",
      "css": ".ds-badge{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;height:22px;padding:0 7px;border-radius:2px;font:600 12px/1 var(--font-sans,'Archivo Variable',sans-serif);color:var(--text-2,#45453f);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--line-2,#b8b8b0);white-space:nowrap}.ds-badge-ok{color:var(--ok,#1b7339);background:var(--ok-soft,rgba(27,115,57,.09));box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb,var(--ok,#1b7339) 45%,transparent)}.ds-badge-warn{color:var(--warn,#9a6200);background:var(--warn-soft,rgba(201,138,0,.12));box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb,var(--warn,#9a6200) 45%,transparent)}.ds-dot{width:7px;height:7px;background:currentColor}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Evidence Chip",
      "kind": "chip",
      "refersTo": "evidence-chip",
      "description": "A fact's source: strength in shape (ring to solid check) and in words.",
      "html": "<span class=\"ds-ev\"><svg width=\"11\" height=\"11\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 12\"><circle cx=\"6\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></svg>driver said</span> <span class=\"ds-ev ds-ev-verified\"><svg width=\"11\" height=\"11\" viewBox=\"0 0 12 12\"><circle cx=\"6\" cy=\"6\" r=\"4.6\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><path d=\"M3.8 6.1 5.3 7.6 8.3 4.6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/></svg>confirmed by provider</span>",
      "css": ".ds-ev{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:5px;height:20px;padding:0 6px;border-radius:2px;font:600 11.5px/1 var(--font-sans,'Archivo Variable',sans-serif);white-space:nowrap;color:var(--text-3,#686862);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px var(--line-2,#b8b8b0)}.ds-ev-verified{color:var(--ok,#1b7339);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb,var(--ok,#1b7339) 45%,transparent)}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Route Strip",
      "kind": "custom",
      "description": "A vertical line of stops; each leg in its mode colour, its pattern saying booked (solid), quoted (dashed) or estimated (dotted).",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-rs\"><div class=\"ds-stop\"><span class=\"ds-node\"></span>Munich</div><div class=\"ds-leg\"><span class=\"ds-rl ds-est\"></span><span class=\"ds-rb\"><b>Drive</b> 20 Oct 13:00 · 10 h 42 min</span></div><div class=\"ds-stop\"><span class=\"ds-node ds-end\"></span>Hamburg</div></div>",
      "css": ".ds-rs{display:grid;font:650 14px/1.4 var(--font-sans,'Archivo Variable',sans-serif);color:var(--text,#111111);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.ds-stop,.ds-leg{display:grid;grid-template-columns:28px minmax(0,1fr);gap:12px;align-items:center}.ds-stop{min-height:28px}.ds-node{justify-self:center;width:13px;height:13px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--surface,#ffffff);box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 3px var(--text,#111111)}.ds-end{background:var(--text,#111111)}.ds-rl{justify-self:center;width:4px;min-height:52px;background:var(--mode-drive,#c98a00)}.ds-est{background:repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom,var(--mode-drive,#c98a00) 0 3px,transparent 3px 7px)}.ds-rb{padding:10px 0;font-size:13px;font-weight:400;color:var(--text-2,#45453f)}.ds-rb b{font-weight:650;color:var(--text,#111111);margin-right:8px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Kursbuch",
    "overview": "**Creative North Star: \"The Kursbuch\"**\n\nBahnOS looks like a rail and ferry timetable book printed on thin paper. Today's work is laid out as a timetable: each order is a row in a fixed column rhythm, and the time left sits right-aligned in tabular figures, like a departure time. Each route is drawn as a vertical line of stops. Type is ink on white. A heavy rule opens every table and section, hairlines separate the rows, and corners are square. Colour is used only where it has a job to do.\n\nThe density is a timetable's: rows of 11px by 16px padding, 14px body text, labels set condensed and uppercase, and no cards floating on a tinted canvas. Depth comes from rules and one reversed plate, not from shadows. Both themes come from the same tokens. In the dark theme the paper turns near-black (#0e0e0d), the ink turns warm off-white, and the rules turn light.\n\nThe system rejects the category default it replaced: rounded grey cards with one soft accent in a sidebar app (ADR-016's look).",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Heavy 2px rule above every table and section, 1px hairlines between rows, square corners.",
      "Archivo condensed (wdth 75) and uppercase for page titles, column heads and labels; normal width for anything people read.",
      "Tabular figures everywhere: body text carries `tnum`.",
      "Ink means act, signal red means needs you or late, and mode colours name the leg.",
      "One reversed plate (ink ground, paper type) marks the selected row in each list, and it slides when the selection moves.",
      "Flat at rest. Shadows exist only on layers that float above the page."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Ink Acts Rule",
        "body": "The primary response fills in ink, never in red. Red marks what needs you, and ink marks what you do about it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Red Is Urgency Rule",
        "body": "Signal Red appears only where something needs a person or is late, plus the brand square and the current-nav line. It never fills a button or decorates a heading.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mode Colour Rule",
        "body": "Mode colours belong to route legs (and to map layers through the Tailwind mapping). They never carry status. A leg's status is carried by its line pattern and its words.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Two Widths Rule",
        "body": "Use the condensed uppercase cut for things that name a column or section. Use normal width for anything a person reads as a sentence. Headlines of cases and decisions are sentences.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Departure Figure Rule",
        "body": "Every time, count and amount uses tabular figures, and the time left in a list is right-aligned.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Page Rule",
        "body": "Anything that sits in the page flow has no drop shadow. A shadow means the layer floats above the timetable.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Opening Rule Rule",
        "body": "Every table, section and list opens with a 2px ink rule (`border-top` or `inset 0 2px 0`). The decision block and the command menu open with a 4px Signal Red rule instead. A decided decision's rule fades to Strong Hairline.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** open every table, list and section with a 2px ink rule and separate rows with 1px hairlines.",
      "**Do** fill the primary response in ink (#111111 light, #efefe9 dark) and show its number key beside its label.",
      "**Do** set column heads, section heads and fact terms in Archivo at wdth 75, uppercase, 750, 0.06–0.07em.",
      "**Do** right-align due times in tabular figures and colour them Signal Red Text only when late or under six hours.",
      "**Do** mark the selected row of a list with the reversed plate, and only that row.",
      "**Do** pair every evidence colour with a shape and a word.",
      "**Do** take colours from the theme tokens so both themes follow. The Tailwind views map their colour names onto those tokens in `map.css`."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** round containers. Section, row and menu corners are 0, and interactive edges stop at 2px. Circles are kept for things that are round in the world: stop nodes, evidence marks and the countdown ring.",
      "**Don't** put drop shadows on in-flow content. Only floating layers (popover, command menu, toast, phone preview) cast a shadow.",
      "**Don't** fill a button in Signal Red or use red for decoration. Red means needs you or late.",
      "**Don't** use a mode colour to say status. Teal is the ferry, not \"on the road\".",
      "**Don't** set sentence headlines in the condensed uppercase cut.",
      "**Don't** add load choreography. The only authored movements are the sliding plate and indicators, plus height-animated disclosure, and all of it honours reduced motion."
    ]
  }
}